[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/comments/3995865303","html_url":"https://github.com/openxla/xla/issues/38597#issuecomment-3995865303","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/38597","id":3995865303,"node_id":"IC_kwDOHyx1PM7uLBDX","user":{"login":"akuegel","id":14309772,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzA5Nzcy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14309772?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akuegel","html_url":"https://github.com/akuegel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akuegel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akuegel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akuegel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akuegel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akuegel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akuegel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akuegel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akuegel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akuegel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-04T07:49:04Z","updated_at":"2026-03-04T07:52:00Z","body":"I am not 100% sure whether on TPU it is the same, but on GPU we would not be able to do scatter in-place if there is a transpose between the parameter and the scatter. So in that sense, I think the function is doing the right thing (at least on GPU). I believe the bug is that this fusion is even created.\n\nTo expand a bit: Scatter in-place means we only write to certain indices of the shape, but leave everything else untouched. If we wanted to fully support a fused transpose, we would on the one hand need to take the transpose into account when computing where to write additional elements, but also need to transpose the \"untouched\" elements. Doing this in-place sounds difficult, and definitely does not work on GPU.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/comments/3995865303/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/comments/3995890977","html_url":"https://github.com/openxla/xla/issues/38597#issuecomment-3995890977","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/38597","id":3995890977,"node_id":"IC_kwDOHyx1PM7uLHUh","user":{"login":"akuegel","id":14309772,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzA5Nzcy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14309772?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akuegel","html_url":"https://github.com/akuegel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akuegel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akuegel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akuegel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akuegel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akuegel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akuegel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akuegel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akuegel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akuegel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-04T07:56:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-04T07:56:27Z","body":"Regarding reshape: Either a reshape is actually just a bitcast (in which case AlgebraicSimplifier is replacing it with a Bitcast), or it is effectively a combination (transpose) bitcast (transpose), so a bitcast with one or two transposes on both sides. So again, we cannot handle the scatter in-place if a non-bitcast reshape is involved.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/comments/3995890977/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/comments/4080164687","html_url":"https://github.com/openxla/xla/issues/38597#issuecomment-4080164687","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/38597","id":4080164687,"node_id":"IC_kwDOHyx1PM7zMl9P","user":{"login":"akuegel","id":14309772,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzA5Nzcy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14309772?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akuegel","html_url":"https://github.com/akuegel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akuegel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akuegel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akuegel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akuegel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akuegel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akuegel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akuegel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akuegel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akuegel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-18T06:54:21Z","updated_at":"2026-03-18T06:54:21Z","body":"I created a separate internal bug for the TPU team so that they can take a look at this. I don't think they monitor the bugs filed here.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/comments/4080164687/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/comments/4203817373","html_url":"https://github.com/openxla/xla/issues/38597#issuecomment-4203817373","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/38597","id":4203817373,"node_id":"IC_kwDOHyx1PM76kSmd","user":{"login":"shreerajshrestha","id":7519311,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1MTkzMTE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7519311?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shreerajshrestha","html_url":"https://github.com/shreerajshrestha","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shreerajshrestha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shreerajshrestha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shreerajshrestha/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shreerajshrestha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shreerajshrestha/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shreerajshrestha/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shreerajshrestha/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shreerajshrestha/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shreerajshrestha/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-08T04:21:39Z","updated_at":"2026-04-08T04:31:26Z","body":"XLA's TPU buffer allocator assigns the same physical buffer to multiple writers in 6 out of 7 compilation variants of a transformer training step. Two patterns: adamw's bias correction exponents (pow.16 written by both pow.20 and pow.17) and tied embedding gradients (scatter-add overwrites live dot_general output). Forward-only inference is clean. The bug is in the allocator, not remat — remat just changes execution order to expose the corruption.\n\nPR (#38607) fixes the scatter-dot tracing path. The optimizer fan-out (`pow.16` aliased by both `pow.20` and `pow.17`) is a separate issue — the allocator assigns two consumers to the same source buffer via `aliasing_operands`, not a tracing failure through `kTranspose`.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/comments/4203817373/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]